{"tool_name":"tiara-metagenomics","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"tiara-metagenomics","home":"https://ibe-uw.github.io/tiara","license":"MIT","summary":"Deep-learning-based approach for identification of eukaryotic sequences in the metagenomic data powered by PyTorch.\n\ntiara \u2013 a tool for DNA sequence classification.\n\nThe sequences are classified in two stages:.\n\nIn the first stage, the sequences are classified to classes: archaea, bacteria, prokarya, eukarya, organelle and unknown.\n\nIn addition to creating the files above, it creates, in the folder where tiara is run, three files containing sequences from sample_input.fasta classified as mitochondria, plastid and prokarya (--tf mit pla pro option).\n\nIn the Polish translation of the Harry Potter book series, the Sorting Hat (which assigned wizards to different houses) was called Tiara Przydzia\u0142u.","addition_date":"2021-03-19T08:56:22Z","last_update_date":"2021-04-23T09:31:06Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:tiara-metagenomics","credit":[{"email":"a.karnkowska@uw.edu.pl","name":"Anna Karnkowska","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"},{"term":"Sequence classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2995"},{"term":"Sorting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3802"}]}],"name":"Tiara","owner":"zsmag19","publication":[{"doi":"10.1101/2021.02.08.430199"}],"topic":[{"term":"Cell biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2229"},{"term":"Gene transcripts","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3512"},{"term":"Metagenomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3174"},{"term":"Model organisms","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0621"},{"term":"Taxonomy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0637"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"Tiara","home":"https://bio.tools/tiara-metagenomics","license":"MIT","summary":"Deep-learning-based approach for identification of eukaryotic sequences in the metagenomic data powered by PyTorch.\n\ntiara \u2013 a tool for DNA sequence classification.\n\nThe sequences are classified in two stages:.\n\nIn the first stage, the sequences are classified to classes: archaea, bacteria, prokarya, eukarya, organelle and unknown.\n\nIn addition to creating the files above, it creates, in the folder where tiara is run, three files containing sequences from sample_input.fasta classified as mitochondria, plastid and prokarya (--tf mit pla pro option).\n\nIn the Polish translation of the Harry Potter book series, the Sorting Hat (which assigned wizards to different houses) was called Tiara Przydzia\u0142u.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tiara-metagenomics/cmd/ibe-uw.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"doi":"10.1101/2021.02.08.430199","ref_count":0,"refs":[]}]}],"readme":false,"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,"license":false,"operational":200,"redirects":[{"status":301,"url":"https://ibe-uw.github.io/tiara/"}],"ssl":true,"ssl_err":null}},"support":{"issue_tracking":{"public_tracker":null,"resolve_time":null}}},{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tiara-metagenomics/lib/ibe-uw.github.io","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"bi